{
  "title": "Salat of وَ وَاعَدْنَا",
  "data": "On each of the first ten nights of Dhul Hijjah, between the Maghrib and Isha prayers, offer a prayer of two units.\nIn each unit, recite [Surah al-Fatihah](A5) once, [Surah al-Tawheed](A116) once, and this verse of [Surah al-A'raf](A11) (7:142):\nوَوٰعَدْنَا مُوْسٰى ثَلٰثِيْنَ لَيْلَةً وَّاَتْمَمْنٰهَا بِعَشْرٍ فَتَمَّ مِيْقَاتُ رَبِّهٖۤ اَرْبَعِيْنَ لَيْلَةً  ۚ\nWA WAA'ADNAA MOOSAA THALAATHEENA LAYLATAN WA ATMAMNAAHAA BI-A'SHRIN FATAMMA MEEQAATU RABBIHEE ARBA'EENA LAYLAH\nAnd We appointed with Moses a time of thirty nights and completed them with ten more, so the appointed time of his Lord was complete forty nights,\nوَقَالَ مُوْسٰى لِاَخِيْهِ هٰرُوْنَ اخْلُفْنِىْ فِىْ قَوْمِىْ وَاَصْلِحْ وَلَا تَتَّبِعْ سَبِيْلَ الْمُفْسِدِيْنَ‏(142)\nWA QAALA MOOSAA LI-AKHEEHI HAAROONAKH LUFNEE FEE QAWMEE WA ASLIH WA LAA TATTABI' SABEELAL MUFSIDEEN\nand Moses said to his brother Aaron: Take my place among my people, and act well and do not follow the way of the mischief-makers.\nIt is also recommended to fast the first nine days of Dhul Hijjah.\nFor the other acts of these ten days, see [First Ten Days of Dhul Hijjah](AC5).",
  "merits": "The reward of offering this prayer is to participate in the rewards of those who go on Hajj."
}
